# Build-context exclusions for Kerdial's root `Dockerfile` (SH-27), the one
# image the project publishes.
#
# The first two entries are the load-bearing ones. Every workspace package's
# `dist/` is gitignored build output, and this repo has already recorded a case
# where a stale local `dist/` made a missing build step invisible (see the CI
# workflow's own "Build workspace" comments). Excluding them here means the
# image can only ever contain output the `build` stage actually produced: if
# `pnpm build` were dropped, the runtime stage's `COPY --from=build .../dist`
# fails the build instead of silently shipping whatever happened to be lying
# around on the developer's disk. Excluding `node_modules` makes the install a
# real `--frozen-lockfile` install of the pinned tree, not a copy of a host
# tree built on some other libc/architecture (`argon2` ships a compiled
# `.node`).
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/

# Test/tooling artefacts — never inputs to a build.
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
web/dev-dist/
web/.vite/
web/e2e/.cache/
*.log

# Secrets must never enter a build context (they end up in layer history).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
